==Polish==

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{inh|pl|sla-pro|*ǫgъrinъ}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{pl-p|'Węg.ry|a=Pl-Węgry.ogg}}

===Proper noun===
{{pl-proper noun|p}}

# [[Hungary]]
#: {{uxi|pl|Mieszkam na '''Węgrzech'''.|I live in Hungary.}}

====Usage notes====
Colocates with {{m|pl|na}} + locative, instead of {{m|pl|w}} and {{m|pl|do}}. However, use of {{m|pl|do}} in sentences such as ''Jadę do Węgier'' (''I'm going to Hungary'') is also acceptable. See [[Appendix:Polish prepositions used with place names]].

